# THEKRA FRONTEND — CODE STANDARDS (Next.js 16 · React 19 · Tailwind v4 · shadcn/ui)

This folder (`frontend/`) is opened as its own Cursor project root. Paths below are relative to `frontend/`
unless they start with `docs/` (which lives one level up, at the monorepo root: `../docs/`).

## Source of Truth (READ BEFORE ANY TASK)

| Question | Authority |
| --- | --- |
| Routes, rendering strategy, shadcn setup, theming mechanism, i18n/RTL, data-fetching layer, build order | `../docs/plan/frontend-plan.md` |
| Visual, motion, performance (Core Web Vitals) and component-architecture standards | `.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc` |
| The API contract the frontend consumes | `../docs/plan/backend-plan.md` §2–§3 |
| General code style, React/TypeScript conventions, scope and git discipline | **this file** |

If this file and `frontend-plan.md` disagree on a concrete decision, **`frontend-plan.md` wins** — follow it and
tell the user about the conflict. Never invent a third option.

**Next.js 16 is newer than most training data.** Per `AGENTS.md`, verify any Next API against
`node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using it. If a plan snippet uses an API the bundled docs mark deprecated
(e.g. `middleware.ts` is now `proxy.ts`; `next/image`'s `priority` is now `preload`), follow the docs and flag
the mismatch to the user. `params`/`searchParams` are Promises (`const { slug } = await params`); use the
generated `PageProps` / `LayoutProps` helpers instead of hand-written route prop types.

---

## Core Principles

- Clean, readable, maintainable code. DRY. KISS — the simplest solution that satisfies the plan.
- Small functions (~50 lines max), one job each. Meaningful names, self-documenting code.
- Comments only for non-obvious decisions (e.g. why a `<bdi>` wraps a reference), never to narrate code.
- Do NOT create `.md` files, `example-usage` files, demo pages, or scratch files unless the user asks.
- Look for an existing component/hook/util before building a new one (see below).

---

## Tailwind v4 (MANDATORY — repo fact)

- This project has **NO `tailwind.config.*`** and must never get one. Tailwind v4 is CSS-first: tokens live in
  `src/app/globals.css` under `@theme inline { … }`, wired through `postcss.config.mjs`
  (`@tailwindcss/postcss`).
- Never follow an older Tailwind/shadcn tutorial that says "add this to `tailwind.config.ts`" or install
  `tailwindcss-animate` (v4 uses `tw-animate-css`). New design tokens go in `globals.css` only, and only when
  the task is a token change (see `frontend-plan.md` §4.4).
- `components.json` keeps `"tailwind": { "config": "" }` and `"cssVariables": true` (§3.1). Do not change them.

## Icons (MANDATORY)

- `lucide-react` is the **ONLY** icon library (it is shadcn's configured `"iconLibrary": "lucide"`).
- Never introduce another icon package (Heroicons, react-icons, Phosphor, Tabler, inline SVG icon sets, …).
- Import named icons: `import { Heart, ChevronLeft } from 'lucide-react'`. Size with Tailwind (`size-4`), colour
  with semantic utilities (`text-muted-foreground`).
- Directional icons (chevrons, back arrows) get `rtl:-scale-x-100`. Decorative icons get `aria-hidden`;
  an icon is never the only accessible label of a control.

## Colors (MANDATORY)

Use ONLY shadcn's semantic, CSS-variable-backed Tailwind utilities:

- Surfaces & text: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-card`, `text-card-foreground`, `bg-muted`,
  `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-popover`, `text-popover-foreground`
- Actions & emphasis: `bg-primary`, `text-primary-foreground`, `bg-secondary`, `bg-accent`, `bg-destructive`
- Lines & focus: `border-border`, `border-input`, `ring-ring`
- Thekra semantic tokens (from `frontend-plan.md` §4.1): `bg-grade-sahih`/`-hasan`/`-daif`,
  `*-intent-sin`, `*-intent-good-deed` — once they exist in `globals.css`
- Opacity modifiers on those are fine (`bg-primary/10`)

**NEVER** a raw Tailwind palette class (`bg-blue-500`, `text-neutral-800`, `border-gray-200`, `bg-white`,
`text-black`) and **NEVER** a literal hex/rgb/hsl/oklch value in a component, `style` prop, or arbitrary class
(`bg-[#0a0a0a]`). The real palette arrives later as a **values-only change to `globals.css`**; one hard-coded
colour breaks that promise and forces a component edit on design day — which `frontend-plan.md` §4.4 defines as
"the component was written wrong".

---

## Use What Already Exists First (MANDATORY)

Before creating ANY new component, hook, util, type, or query key:

1. **Search first** (Grep/Glob), in this order:
   - `src/components/ui/*` — shadcn primitives. The planned batch (§3.2) is: `card`, `tabs`, `command`,
     `dialog`, `sheet`, `badge`, `skeleton`, `sonner`, `separator`, `scroll-area`, `button`, `input`, `label`,
     `select`, `popover`, `tooltip`, `dropdown-menu`, `alert`, `accordion`, `avatar`, `toggle-group`, `form`.
     Use these instead of native `<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>` or hand-rolled modals.
   - `src/components/shared/*` — `AppShell`, `SiteHeader`, `LocaleSwitcher`, `ThemeToggle`, `EmptyState`,
     `ErrorState`, `ArabicText`, and `shared/quote/*` (`QuoteCard`, `QuoteCardSkeleton`, `GradeBadge`,
     `SourceAttribution`, `FavoriteButton`).
   - Sibling `src/features/*` folders and `src/lib/*` (`api/`, `types/`, `query-keys.ts`, `utils.ts`).
2. **Reuse > Extend > Create.** Reuse as-is first; extend with an optional prop second; create only when
   nothing fits. If something is ~80% similar, ask the user before writing a sibling.
3. **`QuoteCard` and friends exist exactly once**, in `src/components/shared/quote/`. Every slice that renders a
   quote — `sin-reminder`, `good-deed-motivation`, `quran-hadith-browser`, `favorites` — imports them. Never a
   per-feature `ReminderCard`/`MotivationCard`/`HadithCard` duplicate.
4. A missing shadcn primitive is added with the shadcn CLI (ask first — it adds dependencies), never hand-written
   into `components/ui/`.

**Anti-overengineering:** don't create a file for one tiny export; don't add a `utils/`/`constants/`/`hooks/`
folder to hold a single value; don't add props, generics or option bags "for later". A constant used by one
component sits at the top of that file. New files are the last resort.

## Component Layering (FIXED — `frontend-plan.md` §3.3)

| Layer | Path | Hand-edited? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Primitives | `src/components/ui/*` | **No.** Generated by the shadcn CLI only. Sole exception: an unavoidable a11y/RTL fix, marked with a comment explaining why. |
| Shared composites | `src/components/shared/*` (incl. `shared/quote/*`) | Yes — cross-feature, presentational |
| Feature components | `src/features/<slice>/components/*` | Yes — flow-specific |
| Routes | `src/app/**` | Routing, metadata, data prefetch and layout composition **only** — no UI logic |

**One-way dependencies: `app → features → shared → ui`.** Never the reverse. `components/shared/*` never
imports from inside a `features/*` folder; `components/ui/*` imports nothing app-specific; a feature slice never
imports another slice's internals — promote the piece to `components/shared/` instead.

Feature folder names are fixed: `sin-reminder`, `good-deed-motivation`, `quran-hadith-browser`, `favorites`.

## Shared Components: Don't Break Existing Consumers

Before editing anything under `src/components/shared/**`: grep every consumer and list them. Changes are
additive — new props default to the old behaviour. If a contract must change, update every consumer in the same
change and call it out. Default fix location for a page-specific bug is the call site, not the shared component.

---

## State & Data (MANDATORY — `frontend-plan.md` §6)

- **TanStack Query v5 for all server state**, through typed hooks per endpoint inside the owning slice
  (`useSins`, `useSinQuotes`, `useGoodDeedQuotes`, `useQuote`, `useFavorites`, `useToggleFavorite`, …).
  Call `useQuery` / `useInfiniteQuery` / `useMutation` directly inside those hooks — there is no custom
  fetch wrapper layer. Hooks return the TanStack result unchanged (no bespoke `{ loading, data }` re-wrapping)
  and contain no JSX.
- Components never call `apiClient` or axios directly — always through a hook. Request functions live in
  `src/lib/api/<entity>.ts`; query keys come only from the `src/lib/query-keys.ts` factory, never inline arrays.
- The envelope (`{ data, meta }`) and error shape are decoded once, in `src/lib/api-client.ts`. UI switches on
  `ApiError.code`, never on message text.
- After a mutation, **invalidate** the affected factory keys (`invalidateQueries` in the mutation's
  `onSettled`) and let TanStack refetch. Using `useQueryClient()` for that one call is fine; manual cache
  juggling (`setQueryData` / `getQueryData` patching, hand-merged lists) is not — the only sanctioned exception
  is the optimistic update in `useToggleFavorite` (snapshot → rollback → invalidate, per §6.4).
- **Zustand only** for the enumerated client-only state: picker open/mode, last-viewed sin/deed slug, variety
  seed (`session-intent.store.ts`), and device preferences (`preferences.store.ts`: `showTranslation`,
  `includeWeakHadith`, `arabicNumerals`, `fontScale`). **Never put API data in a Zustand store.** Theme →
  `next-themes`; locale → `next-intl` + URL; filters/pagination/tabs → URL search params.
- Never read `process.env` in a component — use `src/lib/env.ts`.

## i18n & Content (MANDATORY — a correctness rule, not a style rule)

- All UI chrome text goes through `next-intl` (`useTranslations` in Client Components, `getTranslations` in
  Server Components). **No hardcoded user-facing string** in JSX, `aria-label`, `placeholder`, `title`, or toast.
  `messages/ar.json` is the primary catalogue; add every key to `en.json` too. Never repeat a top-level key in a
  messages file — `JSON.parse` silently keeps only the last one.
- **Content is not UI.** `Quote.textAr` (and every other API content field: `nameAr`, `descriptionAr`,
  `rewardAr`, `narratorAr`, …) is **never** a translation key and is **never** replaced by a UI-locale string.
  It is rendered verbatim from the API response, in `--font-arabic` with `dir="rtl"` on that element. An attached
  `Translation` is shown alongside — beneath it — never instead of it (`frontend-plan.md` §5.5).
- Mixed-direction runs (`Bukhari 13`, `49:12`, emails) are isolated with `<bdi>` where they occur.

## RTL (MANDATORY)

`dir` is set once on `<html>` from the locale. In any shared or direction-agnostic component use logical
utilities only:

| Use | Never (in shared code) |
| --- | --- |
| `ps-*` / `pe-*`, `ms-*` / `me-*` | `pl-*` / `pr-*`, `ml-*` / `mr-*` |
| `text-start` / `text-end` | `text-left` / `text-right` |
| `start-*` / `end-*`, `border-s` / `border-e`, `rounded-s-*` / `rounded-e-*` | `left-*` / `right-*`, `border-l/r`, `rounded-l/r-*` |

Physical utilities are acceptable only inside a component explicitly pinned to one direction (rare — say why in
a comment). Check every UI change in both `ar` (RTL) and `en` (LTR).

## Forms

`react-hook-form` + `zod` via shadcn's `form` primitive (added in phase 4 with the auth screens) for every form.
Never a `useState` + manual validation loop. Every input has a real `<Label>`; errors are tied with
`aria-describedby` and are never colour-only. Build dynamic schemas with `useMemo`.

---

## React & TypeScript Hygiene

- Functional components only; hooks at the top level, never in conditions/loops; custom hooks start with `use`
  and have specific names (`useSinQuotes`, not `useData`).
- One responsibility per custom hook and per `useEffect`. Don't create a hook for single-use logic just to shrink
  a component. Prefer derived values (`useMemo` or plain expressions) over state synced in an effect.
- Components stay under **~300 lines**; split into subcomponents beside them when they grow.
- Server Components by default; add `'use client'` only where interactivity requires it, as low in the tree as
  possible.
- Props: `interface ComponentNameProps` (e.g. `QuoteCardProps`), declared **beside the component in the same
  file**. The backend's "types live only in `dto/`/`entities/`" rule does **not** apply here — don't move a
  component's own props into a `types/` folder. Shared API/domain types (`QuoteDto`, `SinDto`, enums) live once in
  `src/lib/types/` and are imported, never redeclared.
- No `any`, no `as any`; use type guards for unknown data. Enums are `const` objects + union types in
  `src/lib/types/enums.ts` — never imported from `@prisma/client`.
- List keys are stable ids (`quote.id`, `link.id`), **never the array index**.
- Every data-driven view handles **loading, error, and empty** states explicitly (see `design-system.mdc` §5).
- Early returns for edge cases. Make truly optional callbacks optional (`onSelect?: …`, called with `?.()`);
  never pass empty callbacks; never pass a prop equal to its default.
- `useMemo`/`useCallback` where there is real cost (expensive derivation, memoised child, effect dependency) —
  not reflexively. Lazy-load heavy or below-the-fold client components with `next/dynamic`.
- Complete effect dependency arrays; clean up subscriptions/timers; use functional state updates to avoid stale
  closures; never use an unmemoised object/array as an effect dependency.
- `@/` path aliases instead of `../../..` relative chains.

## Naming

- Booleans name the affirmative, current condition with `is`/`has`/`can`/`should` (`isPickerOpen`,
  `hasTranslation`). Never `isNotReady`, `isUninitialized` — name the active state (`isLoading`).
- Composite conditions get a named derived const describing the use-case
  (`const isFirstPageLoading = isPending && !data`), not an inline formula in JSX.
- Handlers: `handle<Event>` inside a component (`handleSelectSin`), `on<Event>` for props (`onSelect`).
- Named constants for magic numbers/strings (e.g. `SEARCH_DEBOUNCE_MS = 300`).

## Security & Privacy

- Never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with API content. Access token in memory only; refresh token in the httpOnly
  cookie (§6.5) — never `localStorage`.
- No analytics or logging event may name the sin a user selected (`frontend-plan.md` §7.1).

## Dead Code

Before finishing: delete unused exports, components, props, types, imports and commented-out code. No "for later"
stubs. Grep every new export — if nothing imports it, remove it.

---

## Scope Control (CRITICAL)

- ONLY modify files the task needs. Don't refactor outside the immediate scope, rename working code, or reformat
  untouched files.
- DO NOT add a dependency without asking. Packages planned in `frontend-plan.md` §8 are added only in their phase;
  `@tanstack/react-query`, `axios`, `zustand`, `tailwindcss` are already present — never re-add them.
- DO NOT modify config (`next.config.ts`, `eslint.config.mjs`, `postcss.config.mjs`, `tsconfig.json`,
  `components.json`) unless the task requires it. Leave the `next dev`-managed block in `AGENTS.md` alone.
- A change to how an API type is read (`src/lib/types/api.ts`) is a contract change — flag it.
- Ask when the plan is silent; state assumptions explicitly; warn about anything outside scope.

## Pre-Push Checklist (MANDATORY)

Work through it explicitly; if a step doesn't apply, say so. Commands run from the monorepo root (equivalent
`pnpm <script>` inside `frontend/`):

- [ ] `pnpm --filter frontend lint` passes (ESLint 9 flat config — the frontend does not use oxlint).
- [ ] `pnpm --filter frontend build` passes.
- [ ] No raw palette classes, hex/oklch literals, `tailwind.config.*`, or non-`lucide-react` icons introduced.
- [ ] No hardcoded UI strings; `textAr` rendered verbatim; logical (RTL-safe) utilities in shared code.
- [ ] Layering respected (`features → shared → ui`); no hand edits in `components/ui/*` without a comment.
- [ ] No API data in Zustand; no direct `apiClient` calls from components.
- [ ] Loading / error / empty states handled; stable list keys; no `any`.
- [ ] `design-system.mdc` "Never do this" checklist passes for every touched component.
- [ ] Checked in both `ar` (RTL) and `en` (LTR) in the browser.
- [ ] No new dependency without the user's approval.
- [ ] No `console.log`, `debugger`, commented-out code, or dead exports.
- [ ] `git diff` reviewed end-to-end: every hunk maps to the task; no unrelated files.

## Git

- Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `style:`, `test:`, `chore:` (optional scope, e.g.
  `feat(sin-reminder): add SinPickerSheet`). No ticket-ID requirement.
- Atomic commits: one logical change each. Never bypass hooks with `--no-verify`.
